## Purpose

This file is the persistent context for AI-assisted work on the EventHub Web App.

It is the single source of truth for:

- current Web App architecture
- current module/page inventory
- mandatory frontend patterns
- backend API integration rules
- participant/organizer auth boundaries
- visual/UI preservation rules
- runtime/environment configuration
- known API contracts
- active mock-vs-real-data state
- recent changes and reasoning

Every meaningful code change must update this file.

A new agent should be able to read only `.agent` and correctly continue the project.

`AGENTS.md` and some leftover `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` files still describe the old Event Spark / Supabase Lovable stack. They are not authoritative for EventHub. This `.agent` file is.

## Project Identity

EventHub Web App is a standalone Vite + React + TypeScript SPA.

The repository originated from a Lovable-generated event application.

Lovable is now the visual/theme foundation only.

Its original backend, Supabase integration, product rules, entities, routes, and business logic are not authoritative for EventHub.

The Laravel EventHub backend is a separate project and is authoritative for API contracts and domain behavior.

Local Laravel project (not modified by this Web App foundation): `C:\Users\Hp\Documents\personal\event management`

